  "stages": [
    {
      "part_no": 1,
      "function_en": "Introduction",
      "function_zh": "引言：破題與定義",
      "language_pattern": "rhetorical questions / X is about ...",
      "source_description": "Micro-Hook: Global context of technology",
      "slides": [
        {
          "slide_no": 1,
          "title": {
            "en": "Micro-Hook: Global context of technology",
            "zh": "全球永續連結"
          },
          "numbers": [],
          "scripts": {
            "A2": {
              "text": "Good morning. Today we look at SDG 9, a world plan from the United Nations. It helps every country build better factories and support modern science.",
              "words": 26,
              "sentences": 3,
              "avg_sentence_words": 8.7,
              "fk_grade": 5.5,
              "speak_seconds_est": 16.4,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B1": {
              "text": "Good morning. The United Nations has given us SDG 9, a goal that pushes every nation towards stronger industry, better networks and the research that keeps them alive.",
              "words": 28,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 14.0,
              "fk_grade": 8.8,
              "speak_seconds_est": 15.3,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B2": {
              "text": "Good morning. SDG 9 is the United Nations framework for industry, innovation and infrastructure, and it commits every member state to upgrading its factories, strengthening its networks and funding the science that development rests on.",
              "words": 35,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 17.5,
              "fk_grade": 12.8,
              "speak_seconds_est": 17.5,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            }
          },
          "authoring": {
            "visual_hint": null,
            "stage_direction": null,
            "target_words": null
          }
        },
        {
          "slide_no": 2,
          "title": {
            "en": "AI as Innovation: Connecting SDG 9",
            "zh": "科技與創新"
          },
          "numbers": [],
          "scripts": {
            "A2": {
              "text": "AI is changing science very quickly. It also changes the way we share our ideas. But the answer always depends on one thing: exactly how we ask.",
              "words": 27,
              "sentences": 3,
              "avg_sentence_words": 9.0,
              "fk_grade": 4.5,
              "speak_seconds_est": 17.1,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B1": {
              "text": "AI has already changed the pace of research and the way scientists talk to each other. But the quality of its answers depends on a single factor: how we phrase the question.",
              "words": 32,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 16.0,
              "fk_grade": 7.2,
              "speak_seconds_est": 17.5,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B2": {
              "text": "Artificial intelligence is transforming research and scientific communication at remarkable speed. But what decides the quality of an answer is not the machine itself — it is the care behind our question.",
              "words": 31,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 15.5,
              "fk_grade": 12.5,
              "speak_seconds_est": 15.5,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            }
          },
          "authoring": {
            "visual_hint": null,
            "stage_direction": null,
            "target_words": null
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_no": 2,
      "function_en": "Problem",
      "function_zh": "問題指認：趨勢與因果",
      "language_pattern": "present progressive for trends / this causes ...",
      "source_description": "Student Experience",
      "slides": [
        {
          "slide_no": 3,
          "title": {
            "en": "Student Experience",
            "zh": "學生生活情境"
          },
          "numbers": [],
          "scripts": {
            "A2": {
              "text": "Many science students use ChatGPT or Gemini. We fix our lab reports, we read short summaries, and we ask about hard homework. It is very quick and easy.",
              "words": 28,
              "sentences": 3,
              "avg_sentence_words": 9.3,
              "fk_grade": 4.9,
              "speak_seconds_est": 17.7,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B1": {
              "text": "As science undergraduates, we lean on ChatGPT almost weekly. It polishes a lab report, shortens a long article, or explains a concept that our lecture notes left unclear.",
              "words": 28,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 14.0,
              "fk_grade": 8.8,
              "speak_seconds_est": 15.3,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B2": {
              "text": "University science majors now delegate whole tasks to ChatGPT, asking it to draft a laboratory report or condense a journal article. Concepts that a lecture left unexplained are handed over too.",
              "words": 31,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 15.5,
              "fk_grade": 11.8,
              "speak_seconds_est": 15.5,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            }
          },
          "authoring": {
            "visual_hint": null,
            "stage_direction": null,
            "target_words": null
          }
        },
        {
          "slide_no": 4,
          "title": {
            "en": "Contextualized Problem",
            "zh": "脈絡化問題"
          },
          "numbers": [],
          "scripts": {
            "A2": {
              "text": "This tool is really handy. But some students only type a few lazy words, and the reply is boring and empty. People call this AI slop.",
              "words": 26,
              "sentences": 3,
              "avg_sentence_words": 8.7,
              "fk_grade": 3.7,
              "speak_seconds_est": 16.4,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B1": {
              "text": "Speed is not the problem. If we ask for something useful without supplying any detail, the reply will be vague and repetitive, and people now call that output AI slop.",
              "words": 30,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 15.0,
              "fk_grade": 8.0,
              "speak_seconds_est": 16.4,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B2": {
              "text": "The technology is quick and convenient, although a request written in five seconds tends to earn an equally unremarkable reply. Vague, repetitive output of that kind is dismissed as AI slop.",
              "words": 31,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 15.5,
              "fk_grade": 10.6,
              "speak_seconds_est": 15.5,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            }
          },
          "authoring": {
            "visual_hint": null,
            "stage_direction": null,
            "target_words": null
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_no": 3,
      "function_en": "Achievements",
      "function_zh": "成果：舉證與比較",
      "language_pattern": "present perfect / comparatives",
      "source_description": "Scientific Explanation",
      "slides": [
        {
          "slide_no": 5,
          "title": {
            "en": "Scientific Explanation",
            "zh": "解釋科學原理 WHY"
          },
          "numbers": [],
          "scripts": {
            "A2": {
              "text": "Why does this happen? The computer never reads your mind, because it only sees the words in your prompt. Few details always bring a weak answer.",
              "words": 26,
              "sentences": 3,
              "avg_sentence_words": 8.7,
              "fk_grade": 3.7,
              "speak_seconds_est": 16.4,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B1": {
              "text": "The system cannot guess our intentions. It predicts an answer from the words we typed and from the patterns in its training data, so a thin prompt produces a thin result.",
              "words": 31,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 15.5,
              "fk_grade": 7.2,
              "speak_seconds_est": 16.9,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B2": {
              "text": "The reason is mechanical. A model cannot infer an intention that was left unstated, so it generates the most probable continuation of whatever context you supplied, and thin context yields a thin answer.",
              "words": 33,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 16.5,
              "fk_grade": 11.6,
              "speak_seconds_est": 16.5,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            }
          },
          "authoring": {
            "visual_hint": null,
            "stage_direction": null,
            "target_words": null
          }
        },
        {
          "slide_no": 6,
          "title": {
            "en": "Scientific Explanation",
            "zh": "解釋科學原理 HOW"
          },
          "numbers": [],
          "scripts": {
            "A2": {
              "text": "A useful prompt has four parts. Give the model a role, and give it the background facts. Then add your goal and a simple limit.",
              "words": 25,
              "sentences": 3,
              "avg_sentence_words": 8.3,
              "fk_grade": 2.8,
              "speak_seconds_est": 15.8,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B1": {
              "text": "A strong prompt carries four things: a role for the model, the background it needs, a precise goal and a realistic limit. Clearer instructions reliably produce a more useful reply.",
              "words": 30,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 15.0,
              "fk_grade": 8.7,
              "speak_seconds_est": 16.4,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B2": {
              "text": "A well-constructed prompt therefore carries four elements. Name the role the model should adopt, supply the background it cannot possibly guess, specify the objective, and set the limitations it must respect.",
              "words": 31,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 15.5,
              "fk_grade": 11.4,
              "speak_seconds_est": 15.5,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            }
          },
          "authoring": {
            "visual_hint": null,
            "stage_direction": null,
            "target_words": null
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_no": 4,
      "function_en": "Solutions",
      "function_zh": "解方：做法與取捨",
      "language_pattern": "instead of + V-ing / modal verbs",
      "source_description": "Impact on Science",
      "slides": [
        {
          "slide_no": 7,
          "title": {
            "en": "Impact on Science",
            "zh": "學術研究衝擊"
          },
          "numbers": [],
          "scripts": {
            "A2": {
              "text": "Clear writing really matters in science. A careful prompt improves the lab reports and the talks that we hand in. Our study also gets quicker and more correct.",
              "words": 28,
              "sentences": 3,
              "avg_sentence_words": 9.3,
              "fk_grade": 4.9,
              "speak_seconds_est": 17.7,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B1": {
              "text": "In research, exact communication matters more than people think. A student who writes good prompts will produce a faster literature review, a tidier lab report and a clearer talk.",
              "words": 29,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 14.5,
              "fk_grade": 9.6,
              "speak_seconds_est": 15.8,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B2": {
              "text": "Precision in scientific communication is not a stylistic luxury. A student who learns to specify exactly what is needed will produce a faster literature review, a cleaner laboratory report and a clearer set of presentations.",
              "words": 35,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 17.5,
              "fk_grade": 14.5,
              "speak_seconds_est": 17.5,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            }
          },
          "authoring": {
            "visual_hint": null,
            "stage_direction": null,
            "target_words": null
          }
        },
        {
          "slide_no": 8,
          "title": {
            "en": "Impact on Society",
            "zh": "大眾社會衝擊"
          },
          "numbers": [],
          "scripts": {
            "A2": {
              "text": "But never copy an answer without thinking. If you do, you will simply stop learning. Real science starts with human wonder, and never with a fast reply.",
              "words": 27,
              "sentences": 3,
              "avg_sentence_words": 9.0,
              "fk_grade": 4.5,
              "speak_seconds_est": 17.1,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B1": {
              "text": "However, if we take these answers without questioning them, we slowly turn into passive learners. Real science has always started with human curiosity, not with an easy click.",
              "words": 28,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 14.0,
              "fk_grade": 8.8,
              "speak_seconds_est": 15.3,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B2": {
              "text": "There is a risk in all this, though. If we accept generated answers without interrogating them, we drift into passive learning, and scientific thinking begins with curiosity rather than convenience.",
              "words": 30,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 15.0,
              "fk_grade": 11.1,
              "speak_seconds_est": 15.0,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            }
          },
          "authoring": {
            "visual_hint": null,
            "stage_direction": null,
            "target_words": null
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_no": 5,
      "function_en": "Implications",
      "function_zh": "影響：推論後果",
      "language_pattern": "first conditional / however",
      "source_description": "AI Literacy Strategy 1",
      "slides": [
        {
          "slide_no": 9,
          "title": {
            "en": "AI Literacy Strategy 1",
            "zh": "AI 素養策略一： 提問前的後設認知"
          },
          "numbers": [],
          "scripts": {
            "A2": {
              "text": "So think before you type. Ask yourself exactly what you really need, and decide who will finally read your report. Then pick the format that fits.",
              "words": 26,
              "sentences": 3,
              "avg_sentence_words": 8.7,
              "fk_grade": 4.1,
              "speak_seconds_est": 16.4,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B1": {
              "text": "So think carefully before you start typing. Decide precisely what information you need, ask who is going to read the answer, and choose the format that suits the task.",
              "words": 29,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 14.5,
              "fk_grade": 7.6,
              "speak_seconds_est": 15.8,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B2": {
              "text": "Only when you have identified your objective does a prompt become worth writing. Ask which information is genuinely missing, who the intended reader is, and what format would communicate it best.",
              "words": 31,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 15.5,
              "fk_grade": 10.6,
              "speak_seconds_est": 15.5,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            }
          },
          "authoring": {
            "visual_hint": null,
            "stage_direction": null,
            "target_words": null
          }
        },
        {
          "slide_no": 10,
          "title": {
            "en": "AI Literacy Strategy 2",
            "zh": "AI 素養策略二： 具體動作"
          },
          "numbers": [],
          "scripts": {
            "A2": {
              "text": "Then give the machine clear orders. Add your student background, and add the exact format you want. Writing a prompt is science communication too.",
              "words": 24,
              "sentences": 3,
              "avg_sentence_words": 8.0,
              "fk_grade": 4.7,
              "speak_seconds_est": 15.2,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B1": {
              "text": "Then hand over a clear set of instructions, including the background of your course and the exact format you expect. Writing a prompt has now become a real part of scientific communication.",
              "words": 32,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 16.0,
              "fk_grade": 8.7,
              "speak_seconds_est": 17.5,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B2": {
              "text": "Then hand over instructions that are organised rather than vague, including your academic level and the exact format you expect. Prompt writing is best understood as a form of professional scientific communication.",
              "words": 32,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 16.0,
              "fk_grade": 12.8,
              "speak_seconds_est": 16.0,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            }
          },
          "authoring": {
            "visual_hint": null,
            "stage_direction": null,
            "target_words": null
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_no": 6,
      "function_en": "Call to action",
      "function_zh": "結語：總結與號召",
      "language_pattern": "to wrap up ... / let's ...",
      "source_description": "The Human Edge: Redefining the human role",
      "slides": [
        {
          "slide_no": 11,
          "title": {
            "en": "The Human Edge: Redefining the human role",
            "zh": "人類獨特價值"
          },
          "numbers": [],
          "scripts": {
            "A2": {
              "text": "Computers can sort a lot of data very well. But they have no wonder, no instinct and no honest heart. Only people really turn numbers into new discoveries.",
              "words": 28,
              "sentences": 3,
              "avg_sentence_words": 9.3,
              "fk_grade": 6.2,
              "speak_seconds_est": 17.7,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B1": {
              "text": "A computer can sort data very well, but it has no curiosity, no instinct and no honest heart. Those human traits are the ones that turn plain numbers into a discovery.",
              "words": 31,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 15.5,
              "fk_grade": 8.3,
              "speak_seconds_est": 16.9,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B2": {
              "text": "Algorithms sort data at a speed no human can match, while remaining incapable of curiosity, of trained intuition and of any sense of duty. Those human traits are what turn raw data into discovery.",
              "words": 34,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 17.0,
              "fk_grade": 11.2,
              "speak_seconds_est": 17.0,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            }
          },
          "authoring": {
            "visual_hint": null,
            "stage_direction": null,
            "target_words": null
          }
        },
        {
          "slide_no": 12,
          "title": {
            "en": "Final Call to Action: The SDG 9 future vision",
            "zh": "最終呼籲與願景"
          },
          "numbers": [],
          "scripts": {
            "A2": {
              "text": "Good ideas always start with good talking. Better prompts bring better answers. But a careful scientist still has to think about every single word.",
              "words": 24,
              "sentences": 3,
              "avg_sentence_words": 8.0,
              "fk_grade": 5.7,
              "speak_seconds_est": 15.2,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B1": {
              "text": "Responsible innovation under SDG 9 starts with responsible talk. Better prompts will bring you better answers, but only a good scientist can turn those answers into knowledge that other people trust.",
              "words": 31,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 15.5,
              "fk_grade": 9.9,
              "speak_seconds_est": 16.9,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            },
            "B2": {
              "text": "Responsible innovation under SDG 9 begins with responsible communication. Better prompts may produce better answers, but knowledge that other people can rely on is made by scientists who question what they are given.",
              "words": 33,
              "sentences": 2,
              "avg_sentence_words": 16.5,
              "fk_grade": 11.9,
              "speak_seconds_est": 16.5,
              "fits_20s": true,
              "provenance": "authored-replacement"
            }
          },
          "authoring": {
            "visual_hint": null,
